// error
// #3427: the retired word below was the bootstrap-bridge spelling of `class`
// (#3425) for exactly one release, so compiler source still built by the
// previous stage0 (which parsed only the old spelling) kept compiling until
// a release carrying `class` existed and the pin moved. The bridge is now
// closed: the old word lexes as an ordinary identifier, not a keyword.
// Dropping the lexer alias alone would leave a user with pre-#3427 source
// facing a generic "expected a top-level declaration" pointing at the word
// they wrote in good faith — the checker instead names `class` as the
// replacement.
//
// What must STAY legal, in the same file: `class Point { x: f64 }`, entirely
// unaffected by the removal.
struct Old {
  x: f64,
}

class Point { x: f64 }

fn main() {
}
